Subject: webshortcuts KCM: a page just loaded has nothing to save

FilterOptions::load() sets the default engine, the two check boxes and
the delimiter, and each of those widgets' change signals is connected to
markAsChanged(). Loading the page therefore marked it changed: Reset
and Apply were enabled as soon as Web Search Keywords opened, and
leaving it asked about changes nobody made. load() now ends by
clearing the flag, as save() does after writing.

diff --git a/kcms/webshortcuts/ikwsopts.cpp b/kcms/webshortcuts/ikwsopts.cpp
index f5c16b0..f487858 100644
--- a/kcms/webshortcuts/ikwsopts.cpp
+++ b/kcms/webshortcuts/ikwsopts.cpp
@@ -353,6 +353,7 @@ void FilterOptions::load()
 
     const QString delimiter = group.readEntry("KeywordDelimiter", ":");
     setDelimiter(delimiter.at(0).toLatin1());
+    setNeedsSave(false);
 }
 
 char FilterOptions::delimiter()
